xmodel/grok-normalform-review.md:45:  **What the proof actually does.** §1.2 inspects five consumers (P0/P1, E5F, merge legality, tower arithmetic, coefficients) and says each is a function of (1.2). The coefficient clause is a retention tautology: “anything not proved to disappear remains in `Ω`.” That is valid as a policy and empty as an identification of fields. The checklist also never names WIN / competing-gap comparisons, N2/N3 joint caps, prefix-δ integrality, Q+E5 as distinct from E5F, or chart/scale data consumed by later gluing. Those consumers are covered *if* `Θ` and `Ω` really retain everything they can observe. The theorem gives no independent reason to believe the listed `TowerHistory` / `CoefficientHistory` slots are that complete; it just defines them to be.
xmodel/grok-normalform-review.md:61:  **Strict branch.** `M=1` is absorbing (MP5 / St 8.4). `W(2)={2}`: `Δ | 2` and `Δ≥3` is empty, so no changing clean resonance. Neutral `(κ̄,ρ,w)=(2(u+1),2,2)`. BOOK-N1 (`SHEET6-III.md:121-129`) is `gcd(κ̄,ν)=1` at every `ν≥2` vertex, i.e. `gcd(2,u)=1`, so every multiplier is odd. Entry `P=2` times an odd product is `P₁=2C` with `C` odd, so `v₂(P₁)=1`. Pole-adjacent gap with parent degree 2 is `(ν_X+1)/(2ν_X)`. Independent check: `5/8 > g_X ⇔ ν_X>4`; N1 makes `ν_X` odd, so the in-window family is exactly odd `ν_X≥5`. `ν_X=3` has `g_X=2/3>5/8` and is outside the advertised window. This block is exact.
