xmodel/sol-round5.log:13871:9:5. **DESIGN:** emit only pristine Row 24, Schur its rank-4 ten-variable frontier to at most five residuals, reduce their base coefficients through the cached 509-element (G_{23}), and build the other-35-fiber D23 atlas before launching family-wide D25 solves.
xmodel/sol-round5.log:13891:217:**CONJECTURE K-D25:** if (K) is a genuine depth-ladder component rather than an accidental embedded component, the five Row-24 residuals should again have conormal rank well below five after reduction on each 11-dimensional survivor component. The first discriminating calculation is the generic conormal rank of the reduced Row-24 residuals at the six witnesses and then modulo each minimal component of (G_{23}). Rank 1–2 predicts a 9–10-dimensional D25 projection; rank 5 predicts roughly dimension 6, still not generic emptiness. A D25 kill would require an exceptional nonlinear incompatibility or unit ideal, not merely “five equations.”
xmodel/sol-round5.log:13897:281:> **Target at (p=105337):** every one of the 36 finite radical components has a proper D23 projection of dimension 11/height two, the same initial staircase and conormal-dependency signature, and the uniform rank-4 Row-24 frontier.
