xmodel/sol-round5.log:23434:+> **Target at \(p=105337\):** every one of the 36 finite radical components has a proper D23 projection of dimension 11/height two, the same initial staircase and conormal-dependency signature, and the uniform rank-4 Row-24 frontier.
xmodel/sol-round5.log:23436:+Merely proving the union nonempty adds nothing to the promoted one-fiber result. Build a 36-fiber D23 normal-form/GB atlas first, hash the feature matrices, and search for an explicit transport between fibers. Baselines are about 11 seconds for a D21 fiber and 63 seconds for representative det23; if they persist, the other 35 components cost about 43 minutes serial per prime and about 0.53 GB of bases per prime (about 2.2 CPU-hours and 1.6 GB for all 36 at three primes). Repeat at \(105673\) only after the first atlas is understood. Then specialize the five Row-24 residuals over the atlas and compare \(r\), support, degree, and conormal rank; do not launch 36 D25 F4 jobs before that comparison.
xmodel/sol-round5.log:23449:+# Instrument Round 5: from a D23 fiber to a germ test and D25
xmodel/sol-round5.log:23457:+5. **DESIGN:** emit only pristine Row 24, Schur its rank-4 ten-variable frontier to at most five residuals, reduce their base coefficients through the cached 509-element \(G_{23}\), and build the other-35-fiber D23 atlas before launching family-wide D25 solves.
xmodel/sol-round5.log:23615:+for every depth, and every other purported η component must reduce identically to zero. This is the all-depth cyclic-character/source-generation proof required above, with finite D23/D25 label maps as regressions. There are then no surplus function equations: all 29 \(H_a\) are in the square block, while the orbit/template factorization equations are identities of the parametrization. Radical, saturation, Rabinowitsch, pivot-definition, and `W`-pin rows are base-chart conditions and must not enter \(D\mathcal E_s\). If an emitted Schur/pivot presentation is used instead of reconstructing the source point, it additionally owes explicit localized unit transformations proving equality with \(\widehat I_E\); set-theoretic equality is not enough for this bridge.
xmodel/sol-round5.log:23689:+### 2.3 Does it predict D25?
xmodel/sol-round5.log:23691:+**FACT:** not as a theorem. Row 24 has nine η components and a rank-4 ten-variable first-occurrence symbol, hence at most five existential compatibility residuals. For a fixed full D23 point, only the six new level-56 variables move, their sub-symbol has rank two, and seven residuals can remain. Neither count inherits the D23 height-two result.
xmodel/sol-round5.log:23693:+**CONJECTURE K-D25:** if \(K\) is a genuine depth-ladder component rather than an accidental embedded component, the five Row-24 residuals should again have conormal rank well below five after reduction on each 11-dimensional survivor component. The first discriminating calculation is the generic conormal rank of the reduced Row-24 residuals at the six witnesses and then modulo each minimal component of \(G_{23}\). Rank 1–2 predicts a 9–10-dimensional D25 projection; rank 5 predicts roughly dimension 6, still not generic emptiness. A D25 kill would require an exceptional nonlinear incompatibility or unit ideal, not merely “five equations.”
xmodel/sol-round5.log:23695:+## 3. D25 quotient/Schur compiler and the family lift
