+Every component has the same leading monomial and leading coefficient one, so \(\widetilde G=(\widetilde G_1,\ldots,\widetilde G_{509})\) is a monic componentwise Gröbner basis over $B_{36}$. Store each polynomial as one support skeleton plus a 36-entry coefficient vector. A single leading-monomial index and reduction trace can then execute all components in parallel.
