+# Instrument Round 6: the family D25 decision
+
+## Five-line executive summary
+
+1. **DEFECT RULING:** $E_{29}\neq0$ makes the Euler/Ore derivative one $30\times30$ operator with no free stream; withdraw `e=295` as a value of that operator and retain it only as an archived, unpromoted diagnostic of the obsolete $29\times29$ minors.
+2. **STOP RULING:** the old 1,080 minor certificates do not transfer, but an exact all-input/all-output replay through $t^{40}$ gives \(\ell^+\ge31>11\) at all 36 sampled operators, so the substantive D23 stop survives in corrected form.
+3. **D25 COMPILER:** one exact master emission can cover all 36 atlas fibers over their split finite étale coefficient algebra; it shares Row 24, one rank-four Schur transform, and one monomial skeleton, but it must retain 36 coefficient components and componentwise verdicts.
+4. **DECISION:** family-wide D25 EMPTY unconditionally kills every scoped mod $p$ formal germ; D25 NONEMPTY only deepens survival, while a promoted corrected \(e^+\le12\) would be the decisive germ-track signal.
+5. **POSTERIOR (CONJECTURAL):** I assign 6% to all 36 D25 fibers being EMPTY, 22% to a mixed outcome, 72% to all 36 remaining NONEMPTY, and only about 5% conditional probability of finding corrected \(e^+\le12\) on a D25 survivor.
+
+## 1. Adjudication of the two Round-5 defects
+
+### 1.1 $E_{29}$: exact refutation and the repaired object
+
+**FACT.** The assertion `eta29 == 0` in Round 5 is false. The first term of $E_{29}$ occurs at $t^{36}$, and its derivative is supported on the six residue-four input coefficients at absolute tail level 48. In characteristic zero,
+
+\[
+ \partial_{\mathrm{tf1}_{48}}
+ [t^{36}\eta^{29}]\mathcal E
+ =-\frac{147880611647231905314470776689}{1024}\ne0.
+\]
+
+Its value happens to vanish at every banked witness; that does not permit deletion of its derivative row. The other eta components $E_{30},\ldots,E_{33}$ vanish through the computed band 41, and the remaining mod-6 grading checks pass there.
+
+Put $u=t^6$. The corrected source and target are
+
+\[
+ X=\bigoplus_{q=1}^{30}t^{r_q}k[[u]],
+ \qquad
+ Y^+=\bigoplus_{a=0}^{29}t^{s_a}k[[u]].
+\]
+
+The 30 source streams are the six residues of each of `tf1,tf2,tg1,tg2` and the three even residues of each of `tg01,tg02`. Their shifts remain
+
+\[
+ r_\rho=6+\rho\quad(\rho\ne4),\qquad r_4=16,
+ \qquad \sum_qr_q=288.
+\]
+
+For $0\le a\le28$, retain the Round-5 shifts
+
+\[
+ s_a=6+2((a+1)\bmod3),\qquad s_{28}=16;
+\]
+
+add $s_{29}=36$. Thus \(\sum_{a=0}^{29}s_a=276\). The derivative is now the single square Ore operator
+
+\[
+ L_s^+=D(H_0,\ldots,H_{29})_s
+ \in\operatorname{Mat}_{30}
+   \bigl(k[[u]]\langle\Theta\rangle\bigr),
+ \qquad \Theta=u\frac d{du}.
+\]
+
+There is no candidate free stream, no family of 30 minors, and no minimization over a free-stream index. The completed equation ideal must likewise be corrected to
+
+\[
+ \widehat I_E^+
+ =\overline{\bigl([u^j]H_a:0\le a\le29,\ j\ge0\bigr)}.
+\]
+
+For a causal $30N\times30N$ truncation $M^+(N)$, define
+
+\[
+ \delta^+(N)=30N-\operatorname{rank}M^+(N),
+\]
+
+and define the delayed inverse loss by
+
+\[
+ \ell^+=\min\{\ell\ge0:
+ F^{n+\ell}Y^+\subseteq L_s^+(F^nX)\text{ for every }n\ge0\}.
+\]
+
+Only after an exact Ore normal form proves stabilization to a finite defect $d^+$ may one record the index diagnostic
+
+\[
+ (e^+)^{\mathrm{idx}}
+ =6d^++\sum_as_a-\sum_qr_q
+ =6d^+-12.                                      \tag{1}
+\]
+
+Equation (1) is not itself a DEPTH $e$. Promotion still requires a causal delayed parametrix, the completed-ideal/source-generation bridge, the quadratic remainder estimate, and **CONJECTURE E-HENSEL** (or an admissible nonlinear coordinate change eliminating the Euler terms).
+
+**REQUIRED ALL-DEPTH GATE — CYCLIC-30.** Prove that $H_0,\ldots,H_{29}$ are all the output streams and that every higher eta component vanishes, including the $t^{42+}$ x-side corrections. The current computation is only a regression through band 41. In particular, $N\ge2$ for $H_{29}$ reaches $t^{42}$, so a corrected stabilized $d^+$ cannot be recovered from the present pure-y truncation.
+
+### 1.2 Ruling on `e=295` and the stop rule
+
+**RULING — `e=295` IS WITHDRAWN FOR THE CORRECTED OPERATOR.** The number 295 was
+
+\[
+ 6\cdot56+r_c-48
+\]
+
+for an old $29\times29$ minor after omitting one input stream. It is neither the value nor a bound for $L_s^+$. The artifact `delta_plus_eta29` is also not a corrected square truncation: it is a $(29N+1)\times29N$ matrix that still omits the selected input. Strictly, no promoted DEPTH $e$ existed even before this correction. Preserve `295` only under a name such as `OLD_29MINOR_E_INDEX`; do not use the derived target $D=591$.
+
+**RULING — THE SUBSTANTIVE STOP SURVIVES, WITH A NEW CERTIFICATE.** A Round-6 read-only replay assembled all 30 inputs and all 30 outputs through global band 40 at the 36 points of 8.S7. The weighted window has 174 output coordinates and 170 input coordinates. Its rank is 117 at 27 points and 115 at nine. In every case, adjoining the unit target supported on $(H_{29},u^0)$, of global level 36, raises the rank by one, so that target is outside the image.
+
+Since $F^6X=X$, the inclusion defining \(\ell^+\) fails at $n=6$ for every \(\ell\le30\). Hence
+
+\[
+ \boxed{\ell^+\ge31>11}
+\]
+
+at all 36 sampled operators. Causality makes this a certified lower bound: inputs above band 40 cannot repair a missing target at band 36, and the $t^{42}$ x-side caveat is irrelevant to this finite-window obstruction.
+
+Replace the statement “all 1,080 blocks stop” by:
+
