+
+giving respectively 3, 6, and 18 coefficient classes. This is useful compression, but it is not a reduction to 3, 6, or 18 solver cases: the joint $g_1,g_2$ key determines all four fiber labels and is injective on the 36 fibers. Keep all three $g_i$; the atlas shows that omitting any one changes the ideal even though the three together cut codimension two.
+
+**CONJECTURE D25-TRANSPORT.** There may be a character-diagonal coordinate change transporting every complete D25 fiber to `a00pp`. The class laws and support identity suggest it, but do not prove it. No solver deduplication may use this conjecture.
+
+### 2.2 The family $G_{23}$ cache
+
+Let $e_\lambda$ be the 36 primitive idempotents of $B_{36}$, and align the 509 monic reduced bases using the common monomial order and the atlas's element-for-element support identity. Define
+
+\[
+ \widetilde G_k=\sum_{\lambda}e_\lambda G_{k,\lambda},
+ \qquad 1\le k\le509.
+\]
+
+Every component has the same leading monomial and leading coefficient one, so \(\widetilde G=(\widetilde G_1,\ldots,\widetilde G_{509})\) is a monic componentwise Gröbner basis over $B_{36}$. Store each polynomial as one support skeleton plus a 36-entry coefficient vector. One leading-monomial index can execute all components in parallel; whenever an intermediate coefficient is a zero divisor, split the reduction trace by its idempotent support mask.
+
+This construction does **not** license copying `a00pp` coefficients into the other components. `d23_atlas_p105337.json` contains hashes, statistics, and the $g$-rows, but not the other 35 full basis coefficient arrays. Production must ingest and hash the actual 36 cached bases. Do not assume that the remaining 506 basis polynomials obey the smaller 3/6/18 class partitions.
+
+### 2.3 Build only the full-live pristine Row 24
+
+Use `VDEG_CAP=25`, call the source generator through absolute level 56, freeze the B-side, and retain `PIN42`. Keep **every** D23 lift coordinate and dormant coordinate live. Extract only the nine $k=24$ components of the original series equation. Assert:
+
+```text
+Row 23 == 0
+eta support(Row 24) == {2,5,8,11,14,17,20,23,26}
+frontier ==
