+## 2. Final family-level D25 emission specification
+
+### 2.1 Can one system cover all 36 fibers?
+
+**YES AS ONE EXACT FAMILY OBJECT; NO AS ONE REUSED SPECIALIZATION.** Let
+
+\[
+ B_{36}=\mathbf F_{105337}[\omega_1,\omega_2,\sigma_1,\sigma_2]/
+ (\omega_1^3-1,\omega_2^3-1,\sigma_1^2-1,\sigma_2^2-1).
+\]
+
+At this split prime and the fixed (r_3) embedding used by the atlas,
+
+\[
+ B_{36}\simeq\prod_{\lambda\in\Lambda}\mathbf F_{105337},
+ \qquad
+ \Lambda=(\mathbf Z/3)^2\times\{\pm1\}^2.
+\]
+
+Use
+
+\[
+ A_1=A_{1,0}\omega_1,\qquad
+ A_2=A_{2,0}\omega_2,\qquad
+ HW_i/W_i=h_{32}\sigma_i.
+\]
+
+This ring is the exact disjoint union of the 36 atlas fibers. It permits one source registry, one Row-24 emission, one Schur transform, one reconstruction topology, and one component-vector normal-form compiler.
+
+The atlas coefficient laws become
+
+\[
+ g_3=g_3(\omega_2\omega_1^{-1}),\qquad
+ g_2=g_2(\omega_2,\sigma_2),\qquad
+ g_1=g_1(\omega_1,\omega_2,\sigma_1),
