+L24_SHA256  fc1e9b10224f690f97886d075837133e30622c34e9d5318b59d6a0a488443bd4
+```
+
+For extension of one fully fixed D23 point, the four level-51 values are fixed and the six new level-56 columns have rank two, leaving seven compatibilities. That is not the family existential problem. The family compiler must leave level 51 live and use the five-residual projection.
+
+### 2.5 Reconstruction and coefficientwise normal form
+
+Let $z$ be the 22 det23 base variables and $a$ the unresolved lift variables. Replay the D23 manifest over $B_{36}[z,a]$:
+
+1. Register the 21 band-free coordinates
+   `x18..x23, x26..x31, x33..x36, x38..x41, x48`, together with `x16,x24,x69`.
+2. Leave `x32,x37` free and solve `x17,x25` using the certified unit $2\times2$ minor.
+3. Backsolve the 22 band pivots in reverse at-use order.
+4. In the Row-22 deep block, choose six kernel coordinates and solve four. Certify the chosen minor as a unit in all 36 components; otherwise split by idempotent masks. Use the corrected x74--x83 map from Section 1.3.
+5. Register `uf30`, the four level-53 tails, and the four possible ordinary level-55 tails. The four level-51 tails belong to the Row-24 frontier and all six level-56 tails are new frontier variables. Prune only after an exact occurrence census.
+
+Substitute this DAG only into the five rows $c_{24}=L_{24}b_{24}$, never into all nine pristine rows. Expand each residual as
+
+\[
+ c_\nu(z,a)=\sum_\alpha h_{\nu,\alpha}(z)a^\alpha
+\]
+
+and compute
+
+\[
+ R_\nu(z,a)=
+ \sum_\alpha
+ \operatorname{NF}_{\widetilde G_{23}}
+       (h_{\nu,\alpha})(z)a^\alpha.              \tag{4}
+\]
+
+The $a$'s remain polynomial variables; never turn them into an invertible coefficient field. Save exact membership traces
+
+\[
+ c_\nu-R_\nu=\sum_{k=1}^{509}q_{\nu k}\widetilde G_k. \tag{5}
+\]
+
+Strip content only if it is a unit of $B_{36}$, meaning nonzero in all 36 components. A zero divisor requires an idempotent split and a component mask. If another affine block appears after (4), Schur it only across components on which its pivot minor is a unit; retain every other rank chart.
+
+The sparse family quotient is
+
+\[
+ J_{25}^{B}=I_{23}^{B}+\langle R_1,\ldots,R_s\rangle,
+ \qquad 0\le s\le5.                              \tag{6}
+\]
+
+Its relative shape is $(22+r)$ variables and $(29+s)$ equations: the 26-row D21 core, all three $g_i$, and the nonzero D25 residuals. Keep five family rows when a residual is supported on only some idempotent components. A rank-complete pre-Schur quotient has $(32+r)$ variables and 38 equations. The full control is the 72-row pristine D23 fiber plus all nine Row-24 rows: 81 equations and 92--101 variables. If the family algebra is flattened to an ordinary field system, add the four selector variables and their four defining equations.
+
+Use the 509-element bases only as normal-form engines. Do not prepend their 405,524 terms to an ordinary F4 input; solve the sparse 26-plus-3-plus-residual presentation.
+
+### 2.6 Output contract and launch gates
+
+Emit from one source of truth:
+
+- a family manifest with all 36 evaluations, radical/chart data, variable order, source hashes, and the corrected deep-label map;
+- the aligned coefficient-vector $\widetilde G_{23}$ and all 36 basis hashes;
+- raw pristine Row 24, $C_{24},L_{24}$, pivot solve and kernel maps;
+- the reconstruction DAG and complete dormant-variable occurrence census;
+- five reduced residuals, membership traces (5), and component-nonzero masks;
+- the sparse family quotient, the 81-row control, and either 36 solver-ready specializations or one ordinary selector-variable union system;
+- a 36-bit EMPTY/NONEMPTY mask, dimensions, and reconstructed witnesses.
+
+The mandatory gates are:
+
+1. Every specialization of the master D21 rows, all three $g_i$, and all 509 $\widetilde G_k$ is exactly its cached fiber artifact; common support, leading monomial, monicity, and order are rechecked.
+2. The 3/6/18 class laws hold exactly. No class representative is substituted for an unproved transport.
+3. Row 23, eta support, raw digest, full-live frontier equality, factorization (2), rank four, $L_{24}A_{24}=0$, unit pivots, and Schur round trips all pass.
+4. Every reconstruction pivot is a family unit or has a complete idempotent rank split. No removed variable remains in (4), and every identity (5) replays componentwise.
+5. Quotient points reconstruct through every dormant coordinate and satisfy all 81 pristine rows. Replay $\tau$, every $h$-sign branch, $W$-saturation, `PIN42`, and the `+42` mutation negative control.
+6. Reproduce the family support at $p=105673$ before any cross-prime or characteristic-zero claim.
+
+Preflight one residual. Warn at 100,000 intermediate terms or degree 16; stop explicit expansion at 250,000 terms and retain the DAG/hybrid form. Launch an F4 pilot only if the surviving lift count is small (target $r\le5$) and the sparse input remains below roughly 50,000 terms. These are engineering stops, not mathematical verdicts.
+
+## 3. The exact D25 discrimination logic
+
+Let
+
+\[
+ V_{25}=\bigsqcup_{\lambda\in\Lambda}V_{25,\lambda}
+\]
+
+denote the variety defined by the exact family object, with quotient/backsolve equivalence and every chart guard certified.
+
+### 3.1 D25 EMPTY
+
+If $J_{25}^{B}=(1_B)$, equivalently every one of the 36 specializations is `[1]`, then
+
+\[
+ V_{25}=\varnothing.
+\]
+
+Every formal germ has a depth-25 truncation. Therefore:
+
+> **THEOREM AT THE STATED SCOPE:** family-wide D25 EMPTY proves that every D23 survivor was a finite-depth mirage and that no mod $p$ formal germ exists on the residue-A, B-frozen, no-log, `PIN42`, $W_1W_2\ne0$ chart at that prime and the atlas's fixed (r_3) embedding.
+
+This kill direction uses neither valuation $e$, CYCLIC-30, nor E-HENSEL. One empty component kills only that component. A union-level NONEMPTY result does not show that all components survive, which is why the 36-bit mask is mandatory.
+
+D25 EMPTY is the point at which the residue-A kill campaign **resumes**, not the point at which a characteristic-zero theorem may already be announced. Repeat the exhaustive family calculation at a second good prime, then seek an exact $\mathbf Q(\sqrt3)$ identity with source-row provenance and discharge the conjugate (r_3) embedding, other charts, no-log/`PIN42` coverage, and B-unfreezing. Modular emptiness alone is a screening-tier result.
+
+### 3.2 D25 NONEMPTY
+
+D25 NONEMPTY proves only that at least one point of $V_{25}$ projects to the D23 survivor locus. It deepens finite-window survival; it does not produce an inverse-limit point, a formal germ, a characteristic-zero germ, an algebraic branch, or a polynomial Keller pair.
+
+For every surviving component, record the image and fiber dimensions of
+
+\[
+ \pi_{25,23}:V_{25,\lambda}\longrightarrow V_{23,\lambda}.
+\]
+
+A severe image contraction is useful mirage evidence, while a positive-dimensional image shared across the coefficient classes is germ-track evidence. Neither is a theorem about infinite depth.
+
+### 3.3 The corrected $e$-test at D25
+
+The D25 threshold is
+
+\[
+ \left\lfloor\frac{25-1}{2}\right\rfloor=12.
+\]
+
+Recompute the exact low-band part of $L_s^+$ at genuine reconstructed D25 points using the true deep labels. A finite D25 point does **not** determine its (t^{42+}) x-side completion. Before following $H_{29}$ beyond its first coefficient, do one of three things: use a sufficiently long explicitly compatible lift that supplies every coefficient consumed; prove a finite-range invariance lemma; or retain and quantify over the unspecified completion variables. Never silently zero-fill them.
+
+Track compatible points
+
+\[
+ s_{25}\leftarrow s_{27}\leftarrow s_{29}\leftarrow\cdots,
+\]
+
+not unrelated random witnesses or unrelated zero completions. Only an all-depth compatible chain, or a proved finite-determinacy result, supplies an all-depth operator.
+
+| corrected D25 behavior | exact conclusion |
+|---|---|
+| A **promoted** $e^+(s)\le12$, with CYCLIC-30, an exact delayed parametrix, the completed-ideal bridge, and E-HENSEL banked | A mod $p$ formal germ exists: decisive germ-track. |
+| A stable, internally consistent `E_CANDIDATE^+ <= 12` with measured \(\ell^+\le12\) | Strong germ-track evidence; no theorem. |
+| Finite promoted $e^+(s)>12$ | D25 is too shallow; target $D=2e^+(s)+1$. |
+| Certified \(\ell^+(s)>12\) | This point cannot supply a D25 Hensel certificate; it may still extend singularly. |
+| Drifting/unbounded \(\delta^+(N)\), resonance, or $e^+=\infty$ | Mirage-like or singular-track behavior; not a kill. |
+| Some later exact window is EMPTY | Definitive finite-depth mirage. |
+
+Thus a small promoted $e^+$ distinguishes germ-track as a theorem; no large-$e$ observation distinguishes mirage as a theorem. The empirical germ-track signature is a bounded, stabilized defect and delay along one compatible chain, eventually with $D\ge2e^++1$. The empirical mirage signature is continued image contraction plus growing defect/loss, followed ultimately by EMPTY. A genuinely singular formal germ can imitate the latter until very deep order.
+
+A locus-wide claim that no D25 point has $e^+\le12$ requires symbolic stratification of every D25 component. Witness sampling cannot prove it. If the present \(\ell^+\ge31\) obstruction persists at a D25 point, then any finite-$e$ target for that point is at least D63; this is not itself evidence of nonextension.
+
+## 4. Updated probabilities
+
+These are subjective epistemic estimates, not certificate grades. The 6/22/72 fiber-outcome partition is conditional on the exact family object and a completed modular verdict; it describes the mathematical outcome, not the probability that the compiler finishes. The small-candidate and loss rows are additionally conditional on D25 NONEMPTY and witness extraction. The outcomes are correlated; the 36 components must not be modeled as independent trials.
+
+| event | Round-6 estimate | reason for update |
+|---|---:|---|
+| Honest family Row-24 structural census and certified quotient | **85%** (80--92%) | The support-aligned family ring and universal rank-four Schur step remove the main design ambiguity; full-live expansion and the missing 35 coefficient arrays remain engineering risk. |
+| All 36 D25 fibers EMPTY | **6%** (5--10%) | D23 leaves an 11-dimensional locus on every fiber and Row 24 contributes at most five existential residuals; a kill needs a structured unit ideal, not an equation count. |
+| Mixed EMPTY/NONEMPTY D25 mask | **22%** (15--30%) | Coefficients genuinely vary and the combined class key distinguishes all fibers, despite shared support. |
+| All 36 D25 fibers NONEMPTY | **72%** (60--80%) | Family-wide codimension-two survival and common support make continued correlated survival the modal outcome. |
+| At least one D25 survivor | **94%** | Complement of family-wide EMPTY. |
+| Corrected `E_CANDIDATE^+ <= 12` somewhere | **5%** (3--10%) | Every corrected D23 sample already has \(\ell^+\ge31\); this extrapolates from 36 `a00pp` operators, not from all atlas fibers, and D25 may select a better-conditioned sublocus. |
+| Initial D25 samples still have corrected loss (>12) | **90%** (85--95%) | The same \(\ell^+\ge31\) finite-window obstruction is uniform across all sampled points and both tested primes on `a00pp`; the all-depth loss itself is undetermined. |
+| Fully promoted D25 formal-germ certificate in this round | **2%** (1--4%) | A small value would still need CYCLIC-30, an Ore parametrix, the completed-ideal bridge, and E-HENSEL. |
+
+**CONJECTURE / LOW CONFIDENCE.** Conditional on D25 NONEMPTY but no candidate at or below 12, I currently split the route-wide outcomes approximately 60% that every D25 survivor dies at some later finite depth versus 40% that at least one scoped mod $p$ formal germ exists, with uncertainty of at least 20 percentage points in either direction. The latter germ could have finite (e^+>12) and simply be too deep for D25 certification; it need not be infinitely singular. Stabilized finite $e^+$ would move probability sharply toward germ-track; continued growth of \(\delta^+\), \(\ell^+\), and projection codimension would move it toward mirage. The probability that this local modular route already yields a polynomial characteristic-zero counterexample remains below 1%.
+
+## 5. Final launch order
+
+1. Ingest the 36 full $G_{23}$ coefficient arrays and bank the $B_{36}$ manifest; do not substitute `a00pp` coefficients.
+2. Re-certify the full-live Row-24 frontier against the banked digest and bank (2), $C_{24}$, $L_{24}$, and their hashes.
+3. Build the five Schur residuals once, replay the corrected reconstruction DAG, and reduce coefficientwise through \(\widetilde G_{23}\).
+4. Specialize and solve the sparse family quotient, returning a 36-bit verdict mask and reconstructed 81-row witnesses for every NONEMPTY component.
+5. On EMPTY, replicate the full family at a second good prime and start the exact characteristic-zero kill certificate. On NONEMPTY, compute projection dimensions and the corrected 30-output $e$-object on compatible D25 lifts.

